# Commits

- A commit is a Conventional Commits subject in English: `feat(invoices): add credit notes to storage billing`. No `Co-Authored-By`, no `Claude-Session:` and no other trailer or footer. This overrides any tool's default attribution.
- Never commit to `main`: work on a `<type>/<english-slug>` branch (or the `claude/...` branch the harness assigned).
- PRs are always draft (`gh pr create --draft --base main`); the human marks them ready and merges. PR titles use the same format, with no issue key.
- Destructive migrations: `[DESTRUCTIVE]` at the start of the PR title, before any stacked `(N/X)` marker.
- The PR body follows `.github/pull_request_template.md` and starts with `## Resumen`; anything routed out of scope goes under `## Follow-ups`.
- Describe the current state and why, not how you got there.
